From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:24:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] completers: Word completion from frequency lists, in every
 text field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stevia's default completer, hunspell, corrects spelling: "Wortvervo"
gives "Verantworte", "schreib" nothing. And it only runs where an app
sets the completion hint, which hardly any app does.

The words completer suggests, from three characters on, the most
frequent words that start with what was typed, from the lists of
plinius-words (/usr/share/plinius-words/<lang>.words, NFC, most frequent
first). Matching ignores case and folds ß to ss; a capital first letter
typed stays one. Words the user typed at least twice come first, and
from then on also when they are not in the list (pos-words.c, copied in
by prepare()). Learned words go to $XDG_DATA_HOME/stevia/words/
<lang>.learned (0600); GNOME Settings removes them and raises
org.plinius.keyboard forget-learned-words so a running keyboard forgets
them too. The list loads in a thread: a layout switch never waits.

The plain US layout says nothing about the language someone writes in,
so it completes in the session's language when there is a list for it.

With org.plinius.keyboard word-suggestions on (the default) completion
is enabled in every field of purpose "normal" that is neither hidden
nor sensitive; off, completion-mode decides as before.
